  "Question": "The incenter of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is \\(I\\). Given \\(\\angle A=50^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle B=60^\\circ\\), find the measure of \\(\\angle AIB\\) (in degrees).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "125",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(AI\\) and \\(BI\\) bisect \\(\\angle A\\) and \\(\\angle B\\), respectively. Thus \\(\\angle IAB+\\angle IBA=25^\\circ+30^\\circ=55^\\circ\\), so \\(\\angle AIB=180^\\circ-55^\\circ=125^\\circ\\).",
